Python Time Tracker

Overview

The Python Time Tracker is a command-line application designed to help users record and monitor the time they spend on different activities.

Users can enter their name, specify an activity, start tracking their time, and stop the activity when they finish.

The program calculates the time spent on each activity and provides a daily activity summary.

Features

Start tracking an activity.

Record the user's name.

Record the activity description.

Automatically record the start time.

Stop an activity and record the end time.

Calculate the duration of an activity.

Store activity sessions in a Python list.

Display recorded activity sessions.

View activity information through a menu.

Exit the application.

